.TH CAL 1
.SH NAME
cal \- display a calendar
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cal
[\-jy] [[month] year]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Print the current local month, a selected month and year, or an entire year
when only year is given. Years are 1 through 9999; months are 1 through 12.
-y selects a full current year when no operands are supplied.
-j prints day-of-year numbers.
.PP
This is the upstream BSD-derived calendar: weeks start Sunday and the British
September 1752 reform omits September 3 through 13. Earlier dates follow its
Julian calendar rules; this is not a proleptic Gregorian calendar.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 for invalid operands/options or output failure.
